>
	<p>
		I'm Nikhil Pradhan. I'm from Sikkim, in the Eastern Himalaya, and most of my
		work so far has been setting up systems in places that had none.
	</p>
	<p>
		In 2021 I founded <strong>ApiCare</strong>, a honey business in Sikkim, the
		state of India where all farming is certified organic. We buy from 150+
		smallholder beekeepers and farmers across three districts. I handled the whole
		build: the strategy and daily operations, the farmers and government partners,
		monitoring and reporting, finding funding, and releasing the product. In 2025
		the Government of India (Dept. of Commerce &amp; Industries, Sikkim) selected
		ApiCare as a private-sector training partner under RAMP, a World Bank-financed
		MSME programme. Our supply chain has been through three KPMG audit cycles with
		no findings. Today a team in India runs ApiCare day to day. I advise them on
		strategy and still prepare the reports for ApiCare's partners.
	</p>
	<p>
		Between 2023 and 2025 I also worked as an independent consultant for small
		hotels and homestays in Sikkim and Darjeeling. Most of them had no website or
		online bookings when I started, so I built the websites, connected the booking
		and channel-manager systems, and ran their social media.
	</p>
	<p>
		In 2025 I started the Erasmus Mundus MBA in Impact Entrepreneurship (EMMIE).
		It took me from Zagreb to Vilnius and, in September 2026, to Liège. I graduate
		in December 2026.
	</p>
	<p>
		Alongside the MBA I'm building <strong>FarmLedger</strong>, which is also my
		thesis. It records each sale a farmer makes to customers, businesses and FPOs,
		and AI turns that history into a credit profile a bank could lend against. The
		same records give buyers the traceability that EU rules (EUDR) will require
		from 2027.
	</p>
	<h2>What's next</h2>
	<p>
		I'm looking for digital transformation work: systems, reporting and data,
		ideally where AI is part of the job. I can start an internship now and a
		full-time role from March 2027. I'm based in Belgium and have work permits for
		Belgium and the Netherlands. Later, once FarmLedger is done, I'd like to bring
		this work to digital roles in the development sector.
	</p>
